<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109491" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφήτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φημί</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>suggester, interpreter,
				expounder,</i> esp. of the divine will or judgement, e.g.
				<i>priest who declares an oracle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.235
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μουσάων ὑποφῆται,</span> i.e.
				<i>poets,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				16.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.115
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτέρων ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					22.116
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γλαῦκος . . Νηρῆος ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1311
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Myst.</u>
				5.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				<u>Syn.</u>
				8.2.1
			</span></i>.</div>
